Bes cîkê qaling be, hîn çê... ê... rinde derkave, cîkê
xaltîkê tenik kirî mişkle.
 
But if the skin is thick, it... uh... comes out better,
auntie made the skin thin, [that's the] problem.

150
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:18,000
No gundo hawe, mere kê çi karî bike?
 
Now the village is like this, what work can a man do?

151
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Riziqê way têdaye.
 
Their sustenance is in it.

152
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

153
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Riziqê kesî namîne.
 
No one's sustenance is left behind [unprovided].

154
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

155
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Welle tebê trêjê, purtxal raş dibe.
 
By God, you'd say grapes, oranges are becoming black.

156
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Maşalla xaltîkê, xaltîk ta çikilik çandine?
 
Mashallah auntie, auntie you have planted seedlings?

157
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Avê şirîket tê?
 
Does the company water come?

158
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Heftê çar ro tê.
 
It comes four days a week.

159
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Na, carke tê?
 
No, comes once?

160
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Sê ro.
 
Three days.

161
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Mê?
 
What?

162
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Sê ro berxwe dide.
 
It yields for three days.

163
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Carke tê? Sê ro.
 
Comes once? Three days.

164
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Ewa.
 
I see.

165
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Tim heye, eletûl.
 
It is always there, constantly.

166
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Rinda, ez zanim teye çandine çîçik.
 
It's good, I know you have planted a little.

167
00:12:50,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Ya Allah, Bismillah.
 
Oh God, Bismillah.

168
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Erê havalno livê derê jî, am hatin mala... mala Muxtêr.
 
Yes friends, here too, we came to the house of... the
Mukhtar's house.

169
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Am hatin ma go am istirahet kî xol vir bîbin.
 
We came, we said let's rest here a bit.

170
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,000
E dar kat, merleqe çêbî. Am hatin ma go am istirahet kî xol
vir bîbin.
 
It became late/noon, lunchtime happened. We came, we said
let's rest here a bit.

171
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Dinya jî pir germ bî welle.
 
The weather became very hot, by God.

172
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Emane av gundo banîk e, mala apû Manan, banîk e.
 
Anyway, this village is high up, Uncle Manan's house, it is
high up.

173
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Am li banîkê ne, am neçûne gundê xwarê.
 
We are on the high part, we didn't go to the lower village.

174
00:13:52,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Tame av gundê banîk e, mala apû Manan, banîk e. Am li banîkê
ne, am neçûne gundê avê.
 
Of course, this is the upper village, Uncle Manan's house,
it's high. We are at the high part, we didn't go to the
water village.

175
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Erê havalno, teb'an amkê noko digindî Hûbka kevin, am ji wê
gindî hatin.
 
Yes friends, of course we will now leave the village of
Hubka, we came from that village.

176
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Amkê jî noko derbas gind bin noko, bi mere bin, lextene
xweş.
 
We will now pass through the village, stay with us, [for]
nice clips.

177
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Teb'an birakî kî me jî me xwestî.
 
Of course, a brother of ours also wanted us.

178
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:38,000
[Music playing]
 
[Music playing]

179
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Erê havalno livê derê jî, am hatin ca xaltîkê, dilê me pê ma
bin vêr.
 
Yes friends, here too, we came to auntie's place, our hearts
stayed with us [to come] here.

180
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Hevala xezênê avê, bombe, mêmê xwa dibê bombe yê.
 
The friend of the water tank, bomb, my uncle says it's a
bomb.

181
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Evana badînîm ne?
 
Are these Badini?

182
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
E, mamê xwa şûra me nîvê Erebî ne, nîvê Kurmancî ne.
 
Yes, my uncle, our language is half Arabic, half Kurmanji.

183
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Teb'an a mentîqa Efrîn, ekseriya şûra me wena ne.
 
Of course, the Afrin region, the majority of our language is
like that.

184
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Lûxetî Kurmancî bi şekl am gi waye.
 
The Kurmanji language generally is all like that.

185
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Exlebiya şûra xwa Erebî têdane. Ermenî têdaye.
 
The majority of their language has Arabic in it. It has
Armenian in it.

186
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Tirkî têdaye.
 
It has Turkish in it.

187
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Çunke em cîranê Tirka û Ereba ne.
 
Because we are neighbors to Turks and Arabs.

188
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Çunki am cîranê Tirko, Erebo ne. Maşalla, cawkî xweş e.
 
Because we are neighbors to Turks and Arabs. Mashallah, it
is a nice atmosphere.

189
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Xaltîk gundê we çiqas mal e?
 
Auntie, how many households is your village?

190
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Gundê me teqrîben nîzîka çêl malî ye.
 
Our village is approximately close to forty households.

191
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Çêl mal?
 
Forty households?

192
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Xaltîk miletî xwa gi heye, gi mal e?
 
Auntie, are all the people there, are they all at home?

193
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Gi ne li mal e ne?
 
No.

194
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Gi ne li mal e ne?
 
They are not all at home?

195
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Begî deh dwanzdeh mal ne.
 
Say ten or twelve households are there.

196
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Heta noko, em şeş mal bûn.
 
Until now, we were six households.

197
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Heta berî vê, yani teqrîben zivistanî çûnî, em bûn heft mal.
 
Until before this, meaning roughly last winter, we were
seven households.

198
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Vê... ewê çîçke havîn se çor hatin.
 
This... those few [people] came for the summer, three or
four came.

199
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
E werm, inşalla giya beftin wara.
 
Yes come, God willing they will all come back.

200
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Inşalla.
 
God willing.

201
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
No cema gund gi mal ne.
 
No, the whole village is not at home [inhabited].

202
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Inşalla.
 
God willing.

203
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Bes yek yek hene li derveyî Ewropa ne.
 
But there are ones and twos outside in Europe.

204
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
Wele gundî me ne watin no.
 
By God, our villagers are not like that [no].

205
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Gundî me dernakevin.
 
Our villagers don't come out.

206
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Em nanorin no.
 
We don't stare/look no.

207
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Azanim çêl di nûv gundî wada pirr in.
 
I know forty [households] in your village are a lot.

208
00:19:59,000 --> 00:19:59,000
E her ne.
 
Yes.

209
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
E her ne.
 
Yes, they are there.

210
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Gundê we bi çi tê naskirin? Bi çi me’rûf e?
 
What is your village known for? What is it famous for?

211
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Ne wek cema’et, be’dê no em... simaq e, hejîr e, tiştek wena
neda, me’rûf nîna di tîcaretê da? Cema’et bi çi tê naskirin?
 
Not just the community, afterwards we... is it sumac, is it
figs, isn't there something like that, isn't it famous in
trade? What are the people known for?

212
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Ewa layê min, cema’et... gund bi navê kê ye?
 
Oh my son, the community... who is the village named after?

213
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Gund bi navê Mola Evdik e.
 
The village is named Mola Evdik.

214
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Mola Evdik?
 
Mola Evdik?

215
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Belê. Û Mola Osman Reşik.
 
Yes. And Mola Osman Reshik.

216
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Ew jî kin ne, esas?
 
Are they [relatives] as well, originally?

217
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Ewa la, pîşîvana li Tirkiyê dibê hewatin ne, de negihiştim
gund o.
 
Oh son, the former ones must have come from Turkey, I didn't
reach [that time of] the village.

218
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Li Tirkiyê hatine.
 
They came from Turkey.

219
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Û li viderê yerle bîne.
 
And they settled here.

220
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Em bi xwe, em ne ji vira bûn.
 
As for us, we were not from here.

221
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Kalê min û bavê min... Bavkî Xolfet... bi xol Çema bû, hat
li viderê rûnişt, li vir zewicî...
 
My grandfather and my father... Father Xolfet... was
originally from Chema, he came and settled here, got married
here...

222
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Û li vir yerle bû.
 
And he settled here.

223
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Xaltîk tu bi xwe tu ji vî gundî yî?
 
Auntie, are you yourself from this village?

224
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
No, dêkî min ji vî gundî ye.
 
No, my mother is from this village.

225
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Dêkî te ji vî gundî ye?
 
Your mother is from this village?

226
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Ez bi xwe, eslê me ji Amara ye.
 
As for myself, our origin is from Amara.

227
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Amara?
 
Amara?

228
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Mm.
 
Mm.

229
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Selam û selam.
 
Greetings and peace.

230
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Û eleyke selam, paşê em li Raco rûniştin, qismek opî me wana
li Musakê rûniştin.
 
And peace be upon you, later we settled in Rajo, and a
portion of my uncles settled in Musaka.

231
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Ji Amara ye, ser serî min ser çavê min.
 
She is from Amara, upon my head and upon my eyes [you are
welcome].

232
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Ser çavê te sax be.
 
May your eyes be healthy [thank you].

233
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Amara jî teswîr kir, li werî vê.
 
I filmed Amara too, over there.

234
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Erê, axx le ser dikim.
 
Yes, ah, I watch it.

235
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Xaltîk qişkil te li derva hene?
 
Auntie, do you have children outside [abroad]?

236
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Wele lawkî minî li derva ye.
 
Well, my son is outside.

237
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Ki derê ye?
 
Where is he?

238
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Qîzik minî derva ye, Almanya, qîza min û lawê min ne... ne
çû giştî, Holanda.
 
My daughter is outside, Germany, my daughter and my son
are... no wait all of them, Holland.

239
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Holanda.
 
Holland.

240
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Yê ekîd bila, bila li me ser dikin.
 
The one, surely, surely they are watching us.

241
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
E, li ser dikin, silav bo wan ji yan ne.
 
Yes, they are watching, greetings to them from here.

242
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Û ser çavê min û ehlen we sehlen, ji te ra jî, û wekî gotî
çar parçe Kurdistan ra jî.
 
And upon my eyes, and welcome to you too, and as it is said,
to the four parts of Kurdistan as well.

243
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Û şikirmon ji te me geyora û ser serî min, ser çavê min.
 
And our thanks to you for coming to us, upon my head, upon
my eyes.

244
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Ji layî min ra, û kazabê min Şîrîn ez qurban.
 
To my son, and my insides [beloved] Shirin, may I be a
sacrifice.

245
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Qîza min, lawî min, zavî min, û dost, ehbab, meriv, xismê me
gelek li wêr ne.
 
My daughter, my son, my son-in-law, and friends, loved ones,
relatives, many of our kin are there.

246
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Û selamê me ji geyora hene, û bimînin xêr û xweşiyê da.
 
And our greetings are sent to them, and may they remain in
goodness and happiness.

247
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Û oqbet miletê me be, gi bi fitilin.
 
And may it be the destiny of our people, that they all
return.

248
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Saet xweş. Xaltîk te pir bîr kiriye, te bîrî qişka kiriye?
 
Good health to you. Auntie, do you miss them much, do you
miss the children?

249
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Yarem cûre mare bîr ke zebe neçî.
 
My dear, how can we not miss them, our insides [hearts] are
gone.

250
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Jimeş çûne xaltî?
 
Have they been gone for long, Auntie?

251
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
Awa belkî dabe sê sal, dabe çar sal ne.
 
It has been maybe three years, maybe four years.

252
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Dabe sê sal.
 
About three years.

253
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
Bîdayê şerê li Heleb rabûn hatin.
 
At the beginning of the war in Aleppo, they got up and came.

254
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Qîzkê xaltîkê lê ser kin, dabe sê sal ne...
 
Auntie's daughters, look at her, it's been about three
years...

255
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Wa gundî xwe ekîd nedî ye, hûn yê lê ser kin.
 
Surely they haven't seen their village, you will watch it.

256
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Bes jorkê hat îcaze, ba'dî salekê, du sala li Tirkiyê bû,
hat îcazê.
 
But one came for a visit, after a year, she was in Turkey
for two years, she came for a visit.

257
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:17,000
Û salek zêdetir... def defî du sala du nondo bû, î ne çû
giştî Holanda.
 
And a year and more... almost two years she was inside
[here/Turkey], then she went all the way to Holland.

258
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Xwedê, Xwedê destê xwe ser ra bigre û şerê me jî ji vê ra
hene...
 
God, may God keep His hand over them, and our war is also
from here...

259
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Ji gundî hûpko da, hata Holmonya û Holanda.
 
From the village of Hupko, all the way to Germany and
Holland.

260
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Ya me’feze kin, Rebî alemê, ew demê jî me’feze kin.
 
May He protect them, Lord of the worlds, may He protect
those times as well.

261
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Û bimînin xêr û xweşiyê da, û rizqî genda bol be.
 
And may they remain in goodness and happiness, and may the
livelihood of the people be plentiful.

262
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Zalima me’feze kin. Hewalê xêrxwaz o kin inşela, Rebî alemê.
 
May He [God] handle the tyrants. May He make things good for
the benevolent ones God willing, Lord of the worlds.

263
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:38,000
Amîn, amîn. Saet xweş. Xaltîk maşela du’a li we dike, hewul
no.
 
Amen, amen. Good health to you. Auntie, mashallah, is
praying for you, look at that.

264
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Elhemdulila, Xwedê, Xwedê.
 
Praise be to God, God, God.

265
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike xaltîk.
 
May God prolong your life, Auntie.

266
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Û te û miletê gundî hûpko tev da, gi ser serî me, ser çavê
me ne.
 
And you and the people of Hupko village all together, you
are all upon our heads, upon our eyes.

267
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Tev, tev gundî me jî yarem îşta bidor berî zeytûna ne,
be’îva ne, darva ne, bi mişmişa bûn, noka mişmiş çîkên.
 
All, all our village too, my dear, is now surrounded by
olives, almonds, trees, there used to be apricots, now the
apricots are gone.

268
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Vê miletê hat gihand, du gih çû.
 
These people came and arrived, two [groups/times] went.

269
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Xaltîk jêr va lê binêr, ona gundî wa têbê, ona mewqiyê wa ne
rind e.
 
Auntie, look down there, how your village appears, how their
location isn't good.

270
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
War nof jî, ona mewqiyê wa pir rind e, bes sake gund gi
hember hev...
 
Even inside [the valley], their location is very good, just
look, the villages are all opposite each other...

271
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Gundê Rajo, ona xweş e tebîetê gund.
 
Rajo village, the nature of the village is beautiful like
that.

272
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Wele tu zanî, vê geçê ma, li vê geçê rindtir e.
 
Well you know, this side of ours is better than that side.

273
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Ewa.
 
Indeed.

274
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Vê geçê ma, teb’en, û bidebet jî zêde cî molê me.
 
This side of ours, naturally, and with precision too, it is
mostly our property/place.

275
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Ewa.
 
Indeed.

276
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Û vê molê hewşê me.
 
And this property is our courtyard.

277
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Mewqiyê xwe pir xweşik îbare.
 
Its location is extremely beautiful, essentially.

278
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Saet xweş.
 
Good health [Thanks].

279
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Wele.
 
Indeed.

280
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Xwedê we star bike xaltîk.
 
May God protect you, Auntie.

281
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Te jî, Xwedê we bixeyîrîne.
 
You too, may God grant you good.

282
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Xwedê destê xwe ser ta ra bigre.
 
May God keep His hand over you.

283
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike, silavê te jî gihîştin, mobaşer in.
 
May God prolong your life, your greetings have arrived, they
are live/direct.

284
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Silamê me jî ji geyora hene.
 
Our greetings are also to them.

285
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Are hewul no, evro wekî dibê gundê Hûpko ye, emê noka dilax
tadin, werê çêkin.
 
Yes everyone, today as they say is Hupko village, we will
now shake things up, we will make way.

286
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:34,000
Û emê xone bin, em derbasî gundê Şêx Belo bin.
 
And we will get ready, we will pass to Sheikh Belo village.

287
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Şêx Belo jî jimeş da ji min xwestine bisereha.
 
Sheikh Belo has also been requested from me for a long time,
honestly.

288
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:43,000
Li henderê camê nav pir bî ne, ê me hûr û me va kir, me dî.
Emê inşela wir jî ser va teswîr kin.
 
Outside [abroad] the name of the mosque was very
[common/mentioned], we detailed it and opened it, we saw.
God willing, we will film over there as well.

289
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,000
Axaftin li wir de kêm bî.
 
Speech was scarce there.

290
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,000
Are hewul no.
 
Yes everyone.

291
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:49,000
Wadî cografiya me mentiqa Efrîn.
 
There is our geography, Afrin region.

292
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Çî Rajo vira ye, yê Rajo vira ye, wera ona ber vê kelam no
rûnê.
 
Whether Rajo is here, the one from Rajo is here, come
sitting in front of these stalks like that.

293
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Çawk xwe çêke, Rajo biname.
 
Make yourself comfortable, look at Rajo.

294
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Xaseten wextî kalem şiqin didin.
 
Especially when the wheat stalks make a rustling sound.

295
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Sake, hevo jî geliyê Sorisinê ye, dora darin geliyê
Sorisinê.
 
Look, this is also the Sorisin valley, around the trees is
the Sorisin valley.

296
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Maşela mewqîkî pir xweş e.
 
Mashallah, it is a very beautiful location.

297
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Wele ne rabo mer dimire, ne...
 
Well, neither does a man die from work, nor...

298
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Na xweşî mer dimire. Vê bayî, vê tebîetê.
 
Does a man die from discomfort. [With] this wind, [with]
this nature.

299
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Taba vê gundî dîrok hil na kir ne.
 
However, this village hasn't recorded [its] history.

300
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Gundî dîrok hil na kirin, camê gunda pir gund hene, dîrok
hil kirin, ê karab e.
 
The village didn't record history, regarding village
mosques, there are many villages that recorded history, that
is good.

301
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Vê gundî, û vê gundî hember me...
 
This village, and this village opposite us...

302
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Miletê gund nêşt dîrokê qol kin. Sake dîrokê xwe gehene.
 
The people of the village didn't sit to dig into history.
Look, their history is ancient.

303
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Danî kehreba tewzîh Rajo biye, yekê kehrebê tewzîh kin.
 
Assuming the electricity distribution is Rajo, one to
distribute electricity.

304
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Lê.
 
Look.

305
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Wele m’azat qa noxwe ser o be, bin sersê rûniştî, boyî
henek, hewes bine.
 
Well, if the tool isn't on the head [if there isn't
trouble], sitting under the shade, for coolness, just for
desire.

306
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Lê, m’azat... rob rob, em herin, wext me rin tine.
 
Look, the tool... run run, let's go, we don't have good time
[much time].

307
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Ca xaltîkê rûniştî.
 
See, the auntie is sitting.

308
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Xaltîk dibê ezê qehwê çêkim, min got wextî me tune, emê
herin.
 
Auntie says I will make coffee, I said we don't have time,
we will go.

309
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:04,000
Are hewul no, ber vê bayî henek, wele ez norim.
 
Yes everyone, in front of this cool wind, well I don't know.

310
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Wele dinyo...
 
Well, the world...

311
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Ho de here, germ e, bes vir bilind e, mewqiyê xwe pir henek
e.
 
It is usually hot, but here is high, its location is very
cool.

312
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Xaltîk divê akê qehwê çêkim, ma va na da xwar. Wele dilê mi
pê ma.
 
Auntie wants to make me coffee, we didn't drink it.
Honestly, my heart stayed with it [I regret not having it].

313
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Henek e akê, min vir qehwek vaxwar.
 
It's cool, I would have drunk a coffee here.

314
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Dest kê dike vê.
 
Whose hand does this [who creates this]?

315
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Lao wele el’ezîm.
 
Oh man, I swear by the Almighty.

316
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Kê çi xoro biriye vê dinyayê, kê çi xoro biriye vê dinyayê.
 
Who took what for themselves from this world, who took what
for themselves from this world?

317
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Emrê gi çiye, emrê gi saetek e, saetek.
 
What is all of life, all of life is one hour, one hour.

318
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Bûş e dinya bûş. Malî dinyê pûç e.
 
The world is empty, empty. Worldly wealth is worthless.

319
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Tarûx xwe dikro, derbas kir, ta... liki kêf kir haw, haw
jimarê bimîne, zemanî xweş.
 
You made your history, you passed it, until... whoever had
fun, that, that remains for the count, a good time.

320
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Migo zemanî xweş eke jimarê bimîne.
 
I said a good time remains for the count.

321
00:25:40,000 --> 00:26:00,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

322
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:00,000
[Muzîk - Dengê tembûrê]
 
[Music]

323
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:20,000
[Muzîk - Dengê tembûrê]
 
[Music - Sound of the tanbûr]

324
00:32:57,000 --> 00:33:02,000
Erê bre Emar, em îro hatin mala... apo...
 
Yes brother Amar, today we came to the home of... uncle...

325
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Em hatin hewşa kevnar a pir delal a apo...
 
We came to the ancient, very beautiful courtyard of uncle...

326
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Lê mixabin xaltîka min, xuyaye piçekî nexweş e.
 
But unfortunately my auntie, it appears she is a little
sick.

327
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,000
Xaltîk, tu çawa yî?
 
Auntie, how are you?

328
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Welle, ez nexweş im.
 
Well, I am sick.

329
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Wele hewşeke pir delal e, lê mixabin...
 
By God, it is a very beautiful courtyard, but
unfortunately...

330
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Rengê meqamê nexweşiyê li ser xaltîka me heye.
 
The color (tone) of illness is upon our auntie.

331
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Emê hinekî pê ra bi axivin, înşallah emê dilê wê xweş bikin.
 
We will talk with her a little, God willing we will cheer
her up.

332
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Emê hinekî moralê wê bidinê axînê.
 
We will give her some morale, indeed.

333
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Xaltîk, dengê te nayê min.
 
Auntie, your voice isn't reaching me.

334
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Welle ez nexweş im, halê min tune ye.
 
Well I am sick, I have no strength.

335
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Xwedê şîfayê bide te.
 
May God grant you healing.

336
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Xwedê we razî be, sax bî.
 
May God be pleased with you, be healthy.

337
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:37,000
Tu ji kîjan gundî yî xaltîk?
 
Which village are you from, auntie?

338
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Ez ji Gundê Çeqelma me.
 
I am from the village of Cheqelma.

339
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,000
Ji Gundê Çeqelma?
 
From the village of Cheqelma?

340
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

341
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Tu bûka vî gundî yî yanî?
 
So you are a bride of this village?

342
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Belê, ez bûka vî gundî me.
 
Yes, I am a bride of this village.

343
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Hûn malê kê ne?
 
Which family are you?

344
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:49,000
Em mala... mala Îbişê Elî ne.
 
We are the family of... the family of Ibish Eli.

345
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:50,000
Mala Îbişê Elî?
 
The family of Ibish Eli?

346
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

347
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:53,000
Apo merheba.
 
Uncle, hello.

348
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:55,000
Merheba, ser seran, ser çavan.
 
Hello, upon my head, upon my eyes (You are welcome).

349
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Navê te çi ye apo?
 
What is your name, uncle?

350
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:57,000
Navê min Emar e.
 
My name is Amar.

351
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,000
Emarê kî?
 
Amar of whom?

352
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Emarê... Emarê Îbiş.
 
Amar of... Amar of Ibish.

353
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,000
Gundê Şêx Bilo çend mal e apo?
 
How many houses is the village of Shekh Bilo, uncle?

354
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Gundê Şêx Bilo... welle nêzîkî sî û pênc malî heye.
 
The village of Shekh Bilo... well, it has close to thirty-
five houses.

355
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:07,000
Sî û pênc mal hene?
 
There are thirty-five houses?

356
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:09,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

357
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:11,000
Mekteb, tişt lê hene?
 
Is there a school, things like that in it?

358
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:14,000
Mekteb lê hene, heya sefa şeşa ne.
 
There are schools in it, up to the sixth grade.

359
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Heya sefa şeşa?
 
Up to the sixth grade?

360
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:16,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

361
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Êê... yên navîn û lîse tune ne?
 
Uh... are there no middle and high schools?

362
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Na, tune ne, diçin Reco.
 
No, there aren't, they go to Rajo.

363
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:22,000
Diçin Reco?
 
They go to Rajo?

364
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Belê, diçin Reco dixwînin.
 
Yes, they go to Rajo to study.

365
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Jiyan li vî gundî çawa ye? Av heye, tune?
 
How is life in this village? Is there water, or not?

366
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Welle avê dikirrin, av tune.
 
Well, we buy water, there is no water.

367
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Av tune?
 
There is no water?

368
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Bîr tune ne kekim. Hemû danişk in, çeqelmê tînin.
 
There are no wells, my brother. They are all dry/cisterns,
they bring it from Cheqelma.

369
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Avê ji gundê Çeqelma tînin?
 
They bring water from the village of Cheqelma?

370
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:38,000
Belê, bîr lê heye.
 
Yes, there is a well there.

371
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Hûn naqilê (tankerê) bi çiqasî tînin?
 
For how much do you bring a transport (tanker)?

372
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:43,000
Naqil... bi sê sed û pêncî tînin.
 
A transport... we bring it for three hundred and fifty.

373
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:44,000
Sê sed û pêncî trk?
 
Three hundred and fifty Turkish (Lira)?

374
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Sê sed û pêncî wereqe em tînin, welle.
 
We bring it for three hundred and fifty papers (notes), by
God.

375
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Yanî, mehê çend naqil gerek in?
 
So, how many tankers are needed per month?

376
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Em... nîzamî, nîzamî... em çar naqil gerek in.
 
Us... regularly, regularly... we need four tankers.

377
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Mehê?
 
Per month?

378
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Mehê çar naqil.
 
Four tankers a month.

379
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:57,000
Mehê 40 dolarî av?
 
40 dollars a month for water?

380
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Av, teqrîben hîç buha nîne.
 
Water, roughly, it's not expensive at all.

381
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:04,000
Mehê 40 dolarî av... û îş naşxul e, kar tune gund da.
 
40 dollars a month for water... and there is no work, no
jobs in the village.

382
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Kar tune, welle bê mesele, nîne welle. Ez ne îro...
 
There is no work, by God, without issue, there isn't, by
God. Not just today for me...

383
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:10,000
Xwedê deriyekî xêrê veke înşallah.
 
May God open a door of goodness, God willing.

384
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,000
Înşallah kekim.
 
God willing, my brother.

385
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Xwedê rizqê we bişîne, hem ferehiyê bikeve... gulê gulê
werin cihê xwe, malê xwe lolo.
 
May God send your sustenance, and may relief come... may you
return smiling (happily) to your place, to your home, oh my.

386
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Înşallah, Xwedê heye.
 
God willing, God exists.

387
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:20,000
Allah kerîm e.
 
God is generous.

388
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Apê... gundê Şêx Bilo... xeber nav li ku kirin Şêx Bilo?
 
Uncle... the village of Shekh Bilo... where did the name
Shekh Bilo come from?

389
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Hapo, berê digotin Şêx Mihemed...
 
My uncle, before they used to say Shekh Muhammed...

390
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:30,000
Paşê kirin Şêx Bilo...
 
Then they made it Shekh Bilo...

391
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:33,000
Navê esasî gund gerek Şêx Mihemed be bra.
 
The fundamental name of the village should be Shekh
Muhammed, brother.

392
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Şêx Mihemed?
 
Shekh Muhammed?

393
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:36,000
Paşê lê kirin... Şêx Bilo.
 
Later they named it... Shekh Bilo.

394
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Nav li Şêx Bilo kirin?
 
They named it Shekh Bilo?

395
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Hapo, hono... li ser wî esasî dane.
 
Uncle, there... they named it on that basis.

396
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:43,000
Çi tiştekî dîrokî li vî gundî heye?
 
Is there anything historical in this village?

397
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Welle tiştekî dîrokî... welle, çiqasî dîrokî bîjî...
 
Well, something historical... well, however much historical
you say...

398
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Mantiqa, mantiqa me... simaq e, baîd in...
 
The area, our area... it's sumac, they are remote...

399
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:54,000
Na... ez qesda min ew e... yanî şûnwar, tiştên waha...
 
No... my intent is... I mean ruins, things like that...

400
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Şûnwar... welle, tişt lê tunene.
 
Ruins... well, there is nothing in it.

401
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Rezê mîr, deşta kî ab...
 
The Prince's vineyard, the plain of...

402
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Rezê xelîl begê... xelîl begê...
 
The vineyard of Khalil Beg... Khalil Beg...

403
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Xelîl begê?
 
Khalil Beg?

404
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:02,000
Ê, jê ra dibêjin.
 
Yes, they call it that.

405
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Êê, tiştê waha...
 
Yes, things like that...

406
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Ev hewşa kevnar... ev çiqasî dîroka wê heye?
 
This ancient courtyard... how much history does it have?

407
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:12,000
Kekim, ev hewşa... welle, berî... eger xelet nekim, sê sed
sal heye biro.
 
My brother, this courtyard... well, before... if I am not
mistaken, it has been 300 years, brother.

408
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Nêzîkî sê sed sal e?
 
Close to three hundred years?

409
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:15,000
Sê sed sal...
 
Three hundred years...

410
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Lê min dît li hewşê kevirên wan 1952...
 
But I saw stones in the courtyard [dated] 1952...

411
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Hapo, berî 52ya girtin...
 
Uncle, they built/started it before '52...

412
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Gund hebû, hewş hebû, berî 52ya girtin.
 
The village existed, the courtyard existed, they built it
before '52.

413
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:25,000
Ne emrê kalê te?
 
Not the age of your grandfather?

414
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:29,000
Hapo, mezinên me gotin, weke bavê min, bapîrên min, şexsê we
çawa ne...
 
Uncle, our elders said, like my father, my grandfathers,
people like you...

415
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:32,000
Ew mezin bûn, em piçûk bûn şexsê kekim.
 
They were big, we were small personally, my brother.

416
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:34,000
We çend zarok hene apo?
 
How many children do you have, uncle?

417
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Zarokên me, Xwedê ji te ra bihêle...
 
Our children, may God preserve yours...

418
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,000
Heşt in. Çar kur in, çar keç in.
 
There are eight. Four are boys, four are girls.

419
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:41,000
Çar kur, çar keç in? Maşallah.
 
Four boys, four girls? Mashallah (God has willed it).

420
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,000
Yek li vir e, yê din giş derve ne.
 
One is here, all the others are abroad.

421
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Giş li Ewropa ne?
 
They are all in Europe?

422
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Hemû li Ewropa ne.
 
They are all in Europe.

423
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,000
Welle, Xwedê wan biparêze.
 
Well, may God protect them.

424
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

425
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,000
Kal û pîr li vir mane...
 
The old man and woman are left here...

426
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:52,000
Kal û pîr li vir mane, welle.
 
The old man and woman are left here, by God.

427
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Dewleta me ew e, tirba me ew e.
 
This is our state/wealth, this is our grave.

428
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Xwedê emrê we dirêj bike.
 
May God prolong your life.

429
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:57,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, ser seran hatin.
 
May God be pleased with you, you are welcome (upon our
heads).

430
00:36:57,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Xaltîk, dengê te... tiştek nayê gotin?
 
Auntie, your voice... is there nothing to be said?

431
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:02,000
[Unintelligible/Mumbling]
 
[Unintelligible/Mumbling]

432
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Tu kilamekê, tiştekî, ji me ra nabêjî?
 
Won't you sing a song, something, for us?

433
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Welle ez nizanim.
 
Well, I don't know (how/any).

434
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Welehî ez nizanim.
 
By God, I don't know.

435
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Dengê te xweş e, lê tu naxwazî bibêjî.
 
Your voice is beautiful, but you don't want to say/sing.

436
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:13,000
Welehî ez nizanim.
 
By God, I don't know.

437
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Baş e.
 
Okay.

438
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Xwedê şîfayê bide te.
 
May God grant you healing.

439
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Emê destûra xwe ji we bixwazin.
 
We will ask for your permission (to leave).

440
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:20,000
Îcar emê derkevin, biçin nav gund jî...
 
Now we will go out, go into the village too...

441
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:23,000
Wara çîkî sekin.
 
Come, stand for a bit.

442
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:28,000
Erê xalê Emar, vî darê... em can bofkî ten e...
 
Yes uncle Amar, this tree... we are dear guests... [Note:
Dialect heavy, exact phrasing unclear but implies guest
context]

443
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Xwedê rehetî kî bide, Xwedê emrê dirêj bide.
 
May God give comfort, may God give long life.

444
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:35,000
Maşallah, xalo... nexweş e, qolça şikî ye?
 
Mashallah, uncle... she is sick, is her leg/hip broken?

445
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Erê, Xwedê rehetî yê bide.
 
Yes, may God give relief.

446
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:39,000
Saxbûnê jê ra dixwazim.
 
I wish health for her.

447
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Qolê, cefadî ye welle.
 
Her arm/body is in pain/distress, by God.

448
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Çavê min nabînin.
 
My eyes don't see.

449
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,000
Ha?
 
Huh?

450
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:44,000
Çavê min nabînin.
 
My eyes don't see.

451
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:45,000
Çavê te nabînin?
 
Your eyes don't see?

452
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Aa.
 
Yeah.

453
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:51,000
